我们希望真正理解到这两个内容匹配度很高，尽管它们没有任何共同的词汇。
We'd like to actually understand that that's a pretty good match for that query, even though it has no words in common.

272
00:31:22,510 --> 00:31:37,344
通过深度神经网络，我们可以获得词语的平滑表示，从而知道
“汽车零件”实际上与变速器、换挡、刹车片等事物密切相关。
And so with a deep neural net, we can actually have these nice kind of smooth representations of words where we know that car parts is
actually fairly closely related to things like transmissions and gear shifts and brake pads and things like that.

273
00:31:37,646 --> 00:31:48,324
我们还可以利用深度神经网络来给出一个评分，判断基于文档中的词汇，
该文档与查询中包含的词语的相关性有多高。
And we can actually use a deep neural net to give us a score for how likely it is that this document, given the words in the document,
is related to this query, the words in that query.

274
00:31:49,198 --> 00:31:51,264
这项技术于 2015 年推出。
And this was launched in 2015.

275
00:31:51,630 --> 00:31:57,188
在 Google 搜索排名的数百个信号中，它现在是第三重要的搜索排名信号。
It's now the third most important search ranking signal in Google search ranking out of hundreds of signals.

276
00:31:58,144 --> 00:32:02,144
它现在是我们排名系统中的一个非常重要的环节。
it's a pretty important aspect of our ranking system now.

277
00:32:05,038 --> 00:32:22,724
另一类工作，也就是我们团队最初在抽象机器学习模型背景下做的一些工作，
是旨在根据输入序列来预测输出序列。
The other kind of work, so some work that was done in our group originally in the context of an abstract machine learning model for
transforming one input sequence to predicting an output sequence given the input sequence.

278
00:32:23,406 --> 00:32:30,468
从本质上讲，你希望让输出序列的生成受到所观察到的输入序列的影响。
So essentially you want to condition the generation of an output sequence on the input sequence you've observed.

279
00:32:31,024 --> 00:32:46,660
这听起来有点抽象，但其中一个应用场景是：你想让输出序列（在这种情况下是英语句子）基于
对输入序列（在这种情况下是法语句子）的观察来生成。
Now this sounds kind of abstract, but one area this is useful is you'd like to condition the output sequence, in this case,
an English sentence, on the observation of this input sequence, in this case, a French sentence.

280
00:32:47,024 --> 00:33:00,200
因此，你可以通过观察意思相同的法语和英语句子对，从而建立一个机器翻译系统；
学习到当我在法语句子中看到这些词时，在英语句子的相应位置应该使用这些对应的词。
And so you can essentially produce a machine translation system by observing pairs of French English sentences that mean the same
thing, and then learning that when I see these kinds of words in this French sentence,

281
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:04,740
因此，你可以通过观察意思相同的法语和英语句子对，从而建立一个机器翻译系统；
学习到当我在法语句子中看到这些词时，在英语句子的相应位置应该使用这些对应的词。
I should use these kinds of words in this position in the English sentence.

282
00:33:05,870 --> 00:33:09,680
这个神经网络根本不知道它其实是在做翻译。
And this neural net has no idea that it's actually translating.

283
00:33:09,774 --> 00:33:14,724
它只是学会了如何根据输入序列来转换并生成输出序列。
It just learns to transform to produce an output sequence given an input sequence.

284
00:33:15,726 --> 00:33:21,348
基于生成的第一个词，它可以生成输出序列中的第二个词。
And so conditioned on the first word that it's generated, it can generate the second word in the output sequence.

285
00:33:22,286 --> 00:33:25,988
基于第二个词以及之前所有的词，它可以生成第三个词，以此类推。
Conditioned on the second word, and all the previous words, it can generate the third one, and so on.

286
00:33:26,720 --> 00:33:34,692
然后在推理阶段，你实际上会得到一个关于给定输入序列下可能输出序列的概率分布。
And then at inference time, you actually have a probability distribution over likely output sequences given the input sequence.

287
00:33:35,054 --> 00:33:44,100
因此你可以进行束搜索来探索各种可能性，因为最
可能的目标句子并不一定是从最可能的词开始的。
And so you can do a beam search where you explore the possibilities because the most
likely target sentence is not necessarily the one that starts for the most likely word.

288
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:47,920
对吧？
no?

289
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:58,340
这使用的是 LSTM 表示，即长短期记忆网络单元，最初
由 Sepp Hochreiter 和 Jürgen Schmidhuber 开发。
This is using an LSTM representation, so a long short-term memory cell,
which is originally developed by Sepp Hochreiter and Jürgen Schmidthuber.

290
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:05,892
从本质上讲，这些模型非常擅长记住长距离的依赖关系。
And essentially these models are very good at remembering long distance dependencies.

291
00:34:06,446 --> 00:34:12,719
所以如果我在 20 个词之前看到一个输入词，它们能够很好地保留我见过那个词的信息。
So if I saw an input word 20 words ago, they're good at retaining the knowledge that I saw that word.

292
00:34:14,446 --> 00:34:18,947
我们还能将这项研究应用于另一个领域，即与 Gmail 团队的合作。
So another area we've been able to use this research is in collaboration with the Gmail team.

293
00:34:20,462 --> 00:34:24,676
我们都知道在移动设备上打字有点麻烦，这就是语音识别之所以重要的原因。
We all know that typing on mobile devices is a bit of a pain, that's why speech recognition is important.

294
00:34:25,197 --> 00:34:30,080
而且考虑其他交互模态来简化与设备的交互也是很好的选择。
But it's also good to consider other modalities for making it easier to interact with your device.

295
00:34:30,159 --> 00:34:36,900
至于 Smart Reply，嗯，它最初是我们在 2009 年 4 月推出的一个愚人节玩笑。
And so Smart Reply is, well, originally it was an April Fool's joke that we put out in April 2009.

296
00:34:37,902 --> 00:34:41,252
但在 2015 年 11 月，我们围绕这个功能推出了一款真正的产品。
But then in November 2015, we launched a real product around this.

297
00:34:41,774 --> 00:34:42,692
所以我想这挺不错的。
So I guess that's good.

298
00:34:44,719 --> 00:34:54,639
它的工作原理是接收一封 incoming 邮件，根据邮件内容，
尝试预测你可能想对这条消息做出的回复。
And what this does is it takes an incoming email message, and then given the text of the message,
it tries to predict what are likely responses you might want to give to this message.

299
00:34:54,800 --> 00:35:05,580
在这里你可以看到，这个人收到了一封相当长的邮件，虽然不算特别长，
但如果你得在手机上回复的话就挺长的，系统会预测出几个可能的回复，
And so here you see, this person got this fairly long email, not super long, but long if you have to reply to it on an email,
and it predicts a few likely responses, and you can just click on one, you can send it as it is, you can edit it as you see fit.

300
00:35:05,580 --> 00:35:10,980
你可以直接点击其中一个，或者按原样发送，也可以根据需要进行修改。
And so here you see, this person got this fairly long email, not super long, but long if you have to reply to it on an email,
and it predicts a few likely responses, and you can just click on one, you can send it as it is, you can edit it as you see fit.

301
00:35:11,600 --> 00:35:14,160
这对 Gmail 来说非常棒。
And this has been really amazing for Gmail.

302
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:21,508
现在在收件箱产品中，有 10% 的移动端邮件回复是利用这个 Smart Reply 功能生成的。
Now 10% of mobile responses on email, on the inbox product, are generated with this smart reply feature.

303
00:35:21,998 --> 00:35:23,428
这为用户节省了大量时间。
So that's saving people a lot of time.

304
00:35:23,982 --> 00:35:26,320
它的工作原理是：我们收到一封 incoming 邮件。
And the way it works is we have an incoming email.

305
00:35:26,478 --> 00:35:28,932
你知道，这是我队友从他兄弟那里收到的。
You know, this is one that my teammate received from his brother.

306
00:35:29,326 --> 00:35:34,212
“嘿，我们想邀请你参加 11 月 22 日的提前感恩节聚会，等等，等等……”
Hey, we wanted to invite you to join us for an early Thanksgiving on November 22nd, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

307
00:35:34,542 --> 00:35:41,540
我们有一个小型神经网络来判断：这类内容是否可以生成一个符合逻辑的简短回复？
And we have a small neural net that says, is this the kind of thing where we
can likely generate a short response that would make sense for this message?

308
00:35:42,062 --> 00:35:51,140
如果是，我们就激活一个更大的循环模型，也就是这些序列到序列模型，来尝试生成可能的回复。
If yes, then we activate a much bigger recurrent model, one of these
sequence-to-sequence models, that tries to generate likely replies.

309
00:35:51,374 --> 00:35:54,852
这里显示：‘算上我，我会到的’，或者‘抱歉，我没法参加’。
And here it says, count us in, we'll be there, or sorry, we won't be able to make it.

310
00:35:57,294 --> 00:35:59,280
然后你可以点击其中一个。
And then you can click on one of those.

311
00:36:02,030 --> 00:36:06,532
我们也看到过一些将计算机视觉与语言结合的案例。
We've also been seen cases where we can combine computer vision with language.

312
00:36:07,374 --> 00:36:17,880
基本上，你可以使用序列到序列模型，不再用句子作为输入序列的初始化，
而是利用深度神经网络用图像来初始化。
And essentially you can take the sequence-to-sequence model, and instead of initializing the input sequence with a sentence,
you can initialize it with an image using a deep neural net.

313
00:36:27,118 --> 00:36:29,348
我以为是到 9 点 50 分。
I thought it went till uh 9.50.

314
00:36:31,502 --> 00:36:32,324
噢，上面写的是三点。
Oh, that says three.

315
00:36:34,130 --> 00:36:34,310
好的。
OK.

316
00:36:35,406 --> 00:36:37,540
所以你可以给图像生成描述，这非常令人兴奋。
so you can caption images, which is exciting.

317
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:41,828
我跳过这一段，但基本上你可以生成很棒的模型标注。
And I'm going to skip that, but essentially you can generate nice model captions.

318
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:45,764
翻译是另一个我认为非常令人兴奋的领域。
and translation is another area that I think is pretty exciting.

319
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:55,120
序列到序列的研究在公开数据集上显示出初步迹象，表明可以生成高质量的翻译。
So the sequence-to-sequence work showed initial signs that on a public data set, you could generate good translations.

320
00:36:55,200 --> 00:37:06,180
但我们的生产数据量要大得多得多，而且对于我们中的一些人来说，
并不确定它是否真的能成功部署到翻译产品中。
but our production data sets are much, much bigger, and it was not entirely clear to
some of us that it could actually be successfully deployed in a translation product.

321
00:37:07,150 --> 00:37:20,640
实际上，在与翻译团队合作的过程中，我们在过去几年里推出了一套完全基于序列到序列模型并
结合一系列其他改进的翻译系统，解决了大规模应用中的这些问题。
and actually, in a collaboration with the translate team, we rolled out a translation system based entirely on the
sequence-to-sequence model plus a bunch of other improvements over the last couple of years that addresses these problems at scale.

322
00:37:20,814 --> 00:37:23,780
这就是那个模型，你知道的，它是一个非常复杂的模型。
So there's the model, you know, it's a very complicated model.

323
00:37:24,078 --> 00:37:28,484
它使用了 8 块 GPU 来训练这个非常深的 LSTM 模型。
It uses eight GPUs to train this very deep LSTM model.

324
00:37:28,960 --> 00:37:32,420
它包含一个注意力模型，这是一个很有趣的增加项。
It has an attention model that's been an interesting area to add.

325
00:37:33,040 --> 00:37:34,596
然后它有一个解码器。
and then it has a decoder.

326
00:37:35,502 --> 00:37:42,276
接着它利用数据并行来显著提高训练速度。
and then it uses data parallelism to essentially speed up training.

327
00:37:42,990 --> 00:37:51,364
我们实际上能够大幅缩小旧生产系统与人工翻译之间的差距。
and we're actually able to get to significantly close the gap between the old production system and human translations.

328
00:37:51,982 --> 00:37:59,364
在某些情况下，我们能将旧系统与人工高质量翻译系统之间的差距缩小 87%。
So in some cases, we're able to close the gap by 87% between the old system and human quality translation systems.

329
00:37:59,854 --> 00:38:01,056
这非常、非常重要。
And this is really, really important.

330
00:38:01,216 --> 00:38:05,380
这类翻译质量的提升通常几乎不可能实现。
Those kinds of translation quality improvements don't come along basically ever.

331
00:38:05,696 --> 00:38:09,060
而在这里，我们确实实现了显著的改进。
And here we're able to actually really significantly improve it.

332
00:38:09,536 --> 00:38:21,380
而且我看到另一个趋势是更广泛地使用迁移学习、多任务学习和零样本学习，
即在某些目标任务中你并不一定拥有大量数据。
And we're seeing also another trend, I think, is more widespread use of transfer and multitask learning and zero shot learning,
where you don't necessarily have a lot of data for some kinds of tasks you want to accomplish.

333
00:38:23,930 --> 00:38:29,636
目前大多数模型都是针对单一任务从头开始训练的。
And so currently most models are trained from scratch for a single task.

334
00:38:30,446 --> 00:38:31,684
这相当低效。
And this is pretty inefficient.

335
00:38:31,950 --> 00:38:34,656
在数据上效率低下，因为每个任务都需要大量数据。
Uh data inefficient because you need a lot of data for each task.

336
00:38:34,736 --> 00:38:36,964
在计算上效率低下，因为你是从零开始的。
It's computation inefficient because you start from scratch.

337
00:38:37,454 --> 00:38:44,292
在机器学习专家人力上也不高效，因为解决每一个任务都需要投入大量精力。
It's human sort of machine learning expert inefficient because each task that you try to solve takes a lot of effort.

338
00:38:45,806 --> 00:38:55,844
因此，我们在最初翻译发布几周后的后续工作中展示了的一点是，
我们实际上可以对如何翻译语言进行零样本学习。
And so one of the things we were able to show as follow-on work to the initial translation release a couple weeks later was that we
could actually do zero shot learning on how to translate languages.

339
00:38:56,142 --> 00:39:00,656
对于我们从未见过的语对，我们也能够完成翻译。
Language pairs we'd never observed before, we were actually able to translate.

340
00:39:00,816 --> 00:39:13,910
我们训练了蓝色的英语到韩语和英语到日语，以及韩语到英语和日语到英语的语对，
但随后这个系统就能翻译它从未见过的语对——日语
So we trained on language pairs of English to Korean and English to Japanese, shown in blue,
and Korean to English and Japanese to English, but then this system was able to translate from language pairs it never observed,

341
00:39:13,910 --> 00:39:14,790
我们训练了蓝色的英语到韩语和英语到日语，以及韩语到英语和日语到英语的语对，
但随后这个系统就能翻译它从未见过的语对——日语
Japanese to Korean, Korean to Japanese, and produced pretty serviceable translations in that case.

342
00:39:14,790 --> 00:39:20,004
到韩语、韩语到日语，并产出了相当实用的翻译。
Japanese to Korean, Korean to Japanese, and produced pretty serviceable translations in that case.

343
00:39:20,750 --> 00:39:21,508
这非常令人兴奋。
So that's pretty exciting.

344
00:39:22,958 --> 00:39:27,696
我想跳过这些内容，重点讲一下自动机器学习。
I think I'm going to skip some of this stuff and focus on automated machine learning.

345
00:39:27,856 --> 00:39:31,524
我认为这是一个非常令人兴奋的领域，我将以这个作为结尾。
I think this is a really exciting area, and I'll close with this.

346
00:39:31,696 --> 00:39:37,924
目前解决问题的方法是：你有数据、有计算能力，再加上机器学习专业知识。
So currently the way you solve problems is you have data and computation and you add machine learning expertise.

347
00:39:38,702 --> 00:39:46,948
我们希望将其转变为：能不能用数据和更多的计算量，来减少对机器学习专业知识的需求？
And one of the things we'd like to be able to turn this into is can we take data and use a lot more computation,
but eliminate a lot of the need for machine learning expertise?

348
00:39:47,726 --> 00:39:55,936
我给你们展示一个例子，这是我们小组提交给 ICLR 的一篇论文，
题目是《基于强化学习的神经架构搜索》。
And I'll show you one example of this, which is a paper that's been submitted by our group to ICLR,
called Neural Architecture Search with Reinforcement Learning.

349
00:39:56,016 --> 00:40:03,076
核心思想是：我们将生成一系列模型，训练几个小时，
然后利用这些生成模型的损失作为强化学习信号。
And the idea is we're going to generate a bunch of models, train them for a few hours,
and then use the loss of the generated models as a reinforcement learning signal.

350
00:40:04,622 --> 00:40:10,690
这些是它在一些非常小的任务（CIFAR-10 和 Penn Treebank）中产生的模型。
And so these are the kinds of models it comes up with for some very small tasks, CFAR 10 and Penn Freebank.

351
00:40:11,456 --> 00:40:22,148
这不是人类可能会设计的模型，但在没有任何关于使用何种架构的先验知识的情况下，
它在 CIFAR-10 上达到了非常接近最先进水平的结果。
that's not a model that a human would probably come up with, but it actually comes very close to the state of the art result in CFAR
10 without any knowledge of what architectures to use.

352
00:40:22,606 --> 00:40:26,084
它只是在探索各种架构，并找出哪些效果好，哪些不好。
It just sort of explores architectures and figures out which ones work well and which ones don't.

353
00:40:26,670 --> 00:40:34,596
同样地，对于语言建模任务，上方是普通的 LSTM 单元，而这个是通过这种架构搜索发现的单元。
And similarly, for a language modeling task, that's a normal LSTM cell at the top,
and this is the cell discovered by this architecture search.

354
00:40:35,022 --> 00:40:38,244
这实际上超越了该特定建模任务的最先进水平。
And this actually exceeds the state of the art on this particular modeling task.

355
00:40:40,302 --> 00:40:42,656
这是困惑度，数值越低越好。
this is perplexity, so lower is better.

356
00:40:45,056 --> 00:40:48,996
最后，我们需要更好的计算设施。
finally, we need better computing facilities.

357
00:40:49,422 --> 00:40:50,736
神经网络有两个特性。
neural nets have two properties.

358
00:40:50,816 --> 00:41:03,748
一个是低精度也可以接受，另一个是少数特定操作占据了大部分计算量，
这让我们能够专门针对机器学习和神经网络计算来优化计算过程。
One is reduced precision is okay, the other is a handful of specific operations are make up the bulk of this computation,
and that allows us to essentially specialize computations for doing machine learning and neural net computations.

359
00:41:04,206 --> 00:41:10,148
因此，张量处理单元（TPU）是 Google 设计的定制 ASIC，用于加速神经网络计算。
And so tensor processing units are a custom designed Google ASIC that accelerates neural net computations.

360
00:41:10,736 --> 00:41:12,676
它们已经投入生产使用 20 个月了。
they've been in production use for 20 months.

361
00:41:13,198 --> 00:41:18,116
它们被用于每一次搜索查询，也用于我提到的所有翻译工作，并且还用于 AlphaGo 对决。
They are used on every search query, they're used for all the translation work I talked about, they were used for the AlphaGo match.

362
00:41:23,374 --> 00:41:30,308
嗯，我们仍然在某些方面使用 GPU 进行训练，但对于
部署大型神经网络来说，这是一个非常出色的系统。
well, we still find uses for GPUs for training, for example, but this is a very good system for deploying large neural nets.

363
00:41:31,216 --> 00:41:41,604
嗯，随着我们能够实现更多功能，人们期望计算机完成的查询正变得越来越复杂。
Um so as we're able to accomplish more, the queries that we uh try to accomplish
uh people expect computers to be able to do are getting more complicated.

364
00:41:42,062 --> 00:41:43,556
这里有一些示例查询。
So here are some example queries.

365
00:41:44,462 --> 00:41:47,428
这些眼部图像中，哪一张显示了糖尿病性视网膜病的症状？
Which of these eye images shows symptoms of diabetic retinopathy?

366
00:41:48,206 --> 00:41:50,896
实际上，我们已经能相当好地完成这一项了。
